{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: Site archive row recovery from the foreign-source-unavailable stop, head 646268f7c1393890c6ad00e141ad35892ecb4f0a, tree 8328027147c1571d3b386f162e03c3841ad669a9, branch builder/site-foreign-source-recovery-20261025. Nine commits directly on Main 575c113f, 15 paths, all 15 named by the artifacts. Review request 60043c21, checker promise 09b0e23b, request 501cacd4 (builder promise 47bf1787).\n\nBinding caveat: gs reports request 60043c21, and so this promise, as stale from birth. The cause is the planner's 21:36 supersede 49df080b of 8ced57e3, which lies upstream in 501cacd4's provenance. I raised this with the planner in 67636fce. This verdict is on the content. If gs does not treat it as effective for the landing, I will refile the same text on a live basis.\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; request 501cacd4 and the planner's stop data 245e4a11; the production diff (apps/room/archive.ts, archive-prefix.ts, archive-row.ts, archive-operator.ts, archive-driver.ts, archive-adaptive.ts, archive-build.ts); the four test files and the seal map; the runbook section; then the manifest and the evidence directory.\n\nHead and gate. The gate ran at 89dac632 (tree 0fb2d4aa). The head differs from it only in the primary note and the manifest, so the documents-only follow-up rule applies and no second gate is owed.\n\nWhat the head does:\n1. It records why a source failed. When the Grow host cannot read a source's birth, or reads it but finds no reviewed policy for its pin, it now throws ArchivePrefixStopped with a sourceFailure. That record holds the candidate head, the source's full scope reference, a classification (birth-unavailable or unsupported-policy), and the pin when it fits 128 characters (otherwise pinOmitted). The adaptive, fixed and rebuild paths and the driver carry it into archive-pass-diagnostic-v1 as a new sourceFailure field. The driver records it only while the pass is active; finally clears active before the diagnostic prints, so a late settlement cannot change a finished pass. The record costs 512 metadata bytes and 1,024 input-work units, paid before it is built.\n2. It allows a restart for this stop. archiveRestartEligible is now the one predicate that both the operator's rowDigest projection and ArchiveRows.restart use. It admits limit or foreign-source-unavailable, with no pending Mark, zero attempts, no next time, a layout-2 confirmed receipt, and a stored wake that is present, stopped, not pending, and has no next time. Every other binding is unchanged: repository, format, confirmed receipt, row digest, generation, expiry, one transaction, and a read-only replay of the latest directive.\n\nFit with the hosted row. Per 245e4a11, sc_rzinq shows reason foreign-source-unavailable, pendingMark absent, storedWake {pending false, stopped true, next null}, and restartGeneration 1. The new wake guard costs nothing for real rows: stop() saves through #save, which always writes the wake as stopped true, next null, and pending equal to whether a Mark is pending. Layout and attempts are not in the diagnostic, but rowDigest now appears only when the full predicate holds. After the deploy, a non-null rowDigest on the Site row is the operator's evidence of eligibility, and the runbook's step 1 now requires it.\n\nAcceptance against 501cacd4:\n(1) Trace. The note names entry 1797, its single Room A lane source and that source's supported birth pin (planner capture 88c45c77), and no pending Mark. The historical cause is stated as unproved, not guessed. The data is not shown to be unarchivable, so building was right.\n(2) Recovery path. It is a reviewed restart path with the same identity guards as the limit restart, plus the wake guard. The restart grants nothing: the next pass rediscovers the target and admits every source afresh.\n(3) Witness. In the \"Grow production\" scenario of archive-installed.test.ts, a real delivered Room summary is the candidate, and only the child's nativeBirth RPC is fault-injected. The witness shows:\n- the row stops with foreign-source-unavailable and sourceFailure birth-unavailable, with no write credential and no push for the refused candidate;\n- a second run stays stopped without a directive;\n- an exact directive is applied once, and the generation rises by one with the frontier unchanged;\n- recovery confirms the candidate, and sourceFailure is null;\n- a later candidate with the policy removed stops as unsupported-policy and names the pin, and after the policy is restored it stays stopped until a new directive.\narchive-row.test.ts adds refusals for an absent wake, a non-stopped wake and a pending wake, and a fresh foreign-source restart at generation 2. archive-operator.test.ts checks that rowDigest appears for an eligible foreign-source stop and disappears when the wake is not stopped.\n(4) The note and manifest follow the PD-2 rule (checked below).\n\nArchitecture: sound. One predicate now serves both projection and admission, which removes the risk that the diagnostic offers a digest the restart would refuse. The source-failure record is optional on existing result types and follows the same path as capacityRefusal and fixedFinish. In archive-operator.ts the storedWake read moves before the row read; this changes only the order of two charged reads in a read-only frame.\n\nSecurity: no new authority. Only a deployment directive restarts a row, and it is still bound to the exact row bytes, generation and expiry. A restarted row gets no source, policy or export permission: the witness shows an unsupported pin stopping again after a restart. The new diagnostic fields hold only already-validated public identifiers: head, scope reference, classification, and a bounded pin. They hold no birth body, raw error, URL or credential. The seals for archive-operator, archive-build, archive-driver, archive-row and apps/room/archive.ts reproduce: scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs checks every map entry against sourceSeal and passed 4 of 4 when I ran it in the builder's clean checkout at the head.\n\nSimplification: acceptable, with three nonblocking notes.\n- In apps/room/archive.ts the budget charge comes before the throw. If the budget is exhausted at that point, the pass stops with limit and no sourceFailure, instead of foreign-source-unavailable. Both are restartable, but the operator then loses the classification. If this shows up in a tail, charging only when it fits would keep the reason.\n- The new wake loop in archive-row.test.ts does not include a stopped wake with a next time. The predicate refuses it (wake.next === null), but no case pins that down.\n- The note is 18,491 bytes, within the limit. As with the gate-warning head, most of its evidence prose is about setup history. A shorter account would make the record easier to check.\n\nEvidence, verified by me:\n- PD-2 manifest check. The manifest has sha256 4ec835b698a1c2d94c3058c2440c9b82ba3140054b2ec011e2a6939fde84e5de, the value in the request. It records the qualification, the directory ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-25-site-foreign-source-recovery, checkpoint 89dac632 / 0fb2d4aa, fileCount 151, retention and the withheld items. All 151 files are present, with matching bytes and sha256. There are no unlisted files, and no file or directory has a write bit. All 150 SHA256SUMS lines verify. SHA256SUMS (ed1b628a…) and manifest.json (8d1751bc…) equal the values in the manifest. The primaryNote digest 2cf6ca24… equals the note at the head. Every one of the 18 digests cited in the note names a file in the manifest.\n- Gate 23200: result.json exitCode 0, with expectedHead 89dac632 and expectedTree 0fb2d4aa. gate.stdout.log shows changed files 0, every step at exit 0 including \"notes: 0 warnings\", Node 56, Counting 55, plain 2,816 passed and 1 skipped, and native 771 passed and 2 skipped. gate.stderr.log is empty.\n- Stored-wake control. The mutant returns \"applied\" where \"refused\" is expected, at archive-row.test.ts:484:50. That is the absent-wake refusal in the new loop. The other eight cases pass. I read the records; I did not rerun it.\n- The failed owning runs v1 to v3 and the two failed control starts are kept as failures. The note's combined owning count is labelled as a carry across unchanged inputs, not as a single run.\n- Commit subjects are 75 characters or fewer, and git diff --check is clean over the branch. The head sits on the current Main 575c113f.\n\nLimits, stated plainly. Nothing here proves the historical cause, the hosted layout and anchorsPublished value, or hosted recovery. The note assigns those to the planner's deploy and tail under 501cacd4.\n\nRollout notes for the planner (nonblocking):\n1. Deploy dap-grow with --keep-vars, and read the Site diagnostic before building a directive. rowDigest must be non-null. The directive's generation is the row's restartGeneration, which 245e4a11 gives as 1.\n2. After the restart, check the next pass line. If it stops again, sourceFailure now names the classification and the source, and that decides the next step.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 646268f7 / tree 83280271. The builder lands; the planner deploys.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8648b90fe59961c8ffb165a3e6c712e3589e650a","binding":"assigned","head":"646268f7c1393890c6ad00e141ad35892ecb4f0a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:09b0e23b1239a77de316cfcb9688ca47e781ae0c\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:67636fcee5641d7fb54e94473f3c1e558fe6f845\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:47bf17874679029a50fadb85551a7567bb56fd92\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8763ef1a76129001a1e285babbe2ccf6b2b73399","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:09b0e23b12